    <string-array name="guide">
        <item>## Getting started</item>
        <item>Cashbook keeps one or more independent cashbooks (for example Personal, Office or Shop). Each cashbook has its own accounts — cash in hand, bank accounts, digital wallets — each with an opening balance and opening date.</item>
        <item>## Recording entries</item>
        <item>Tap Add in the bottom bar and choose Income, Expense or Transfer. Amount, date, category and account are required; everything else is optional. Use \"Save and add another\" for quick back-to-back entries.</item>
        <item>An account is where the money is held; the payment mode is how it moved. A UPI payment from your bank account is recorded against the bank account with mode UPI.</item>
        <item>## Transfers</item>
        <item>Use Transfer to move money between your own accounts, for example withdrawing cash from the bank. The source account goes down, the destination goes up, and the total does not change. Transfers are never counted as income or expenses.</item>
        <item>## Bills and receipts</item>
        <item>Attach photos from the camera or gallery, or PDF files, to any entry (up to 10 MB each). Files are stored privately inside the app.</item>
        <item>## Finding entries</item>
        <item>The Transactions tab supports search, filters (date range, account, type, category, party, payment mode, amount, attachments) and sorting. Filter by a single account and sort Oldest first to see the running balance.</item>
        <item>## Balances</item>
        <item>Closing balance = opening balance + income − expenses + transfers received − transfers sent. Balances are recalculated automatically whenever an entry is added, edited, deleted or restored.</item>
        <item>## Reports</item>
        <item>Open Reports, pick a report, choose the period and filters, preview it on screen, then save or share it as a PDF or an editable Excel file. The financial year runs from 1 April to 31 March.</item>
        <item>## Deleting and restoring</item>
        <item>Deleted entries go to the recycle bin (Settings › Recycle bin), where you can restore them or delete them permanently. A transfer is always restored as a whole.</item>
        <item>## Backups</item>
        <item>Settings › Backup &amp; restore creates an encrypted backup file protected by your password. Save it to the phone, an SD card or a cloud drive from the file picker. Keep the password safe — without it the backup cannot be opened.</item>
        <item>## Recurring entries and budgets</item>
        <item>Settings › Recurring entries schedules rent, salary or subscriptions. Choose whether each one is added automatically or waits on the dashboard for Post / Skip. Open any entry and tap Make recurring to start from it. Settings › Budgets sets monthly limits per expense category; the dashboard shows progress for the current month.</item>
        <item>## Automatic backup</item>
        <item>In Backup &amp; restore, choose a folder once (phone, SD card or a cloud drive), set a password and turn on Back up automatically. Cashbook saves a backup daily or weekly and keeps only the latest copies.</item>
        <item>## Security</item>
        <item>Turn on a PIN and, if your phone supports it, fingerprint unlock in Settings › Security. Cashbook never asks for bank passwords, UPI PINs, card PINs or OTPs.</item>
    </string-array>
    <string-array name="privacy">
        <item>## Summary</item>
        <item>Cashbook is an offline app. It has no internet permission, contains no advertising or analytics, and does not collect, transmit or sell any personal or financial data.</item>
        <item>## Data stored on your device</item>
        <item>Your cashbooks, accounts, entries, categories, parties and settings are stored only on this device, in a database encrypted with a key protected by the Android Keystore. Bills and receipts you attach are copied into the app\'s private storage.</item>
        <item>## Information we never ask for</item>
        <item>Cashbook never asks for bank login passwords, net-banking credentials, UPI PINs, debit or credit card PINs, or OTPs. For bank accounts you may optionally enter only a name and the last four digits of the account number.</item>
        <item>## Backups and exports</item>
        <item>Backups are encrypted with a password you choose and are saved only to the location you pick in Android\'s file picker (which may be a cloud drive you select). PDF and Excel exports are created only when you ask, and shared only through the Android share menu when you choose to share them.</item>
        <item>## Permissions</item>
        <item>Notifications: only if you turn on backup reminders. Biometrics: only if you turn on fingerprint unlock. Camera photos, gallery images and files are opened through Android\'s system pickers, so Cashbook does not need storage or camera permissions.</item>
        <item>## Deleting your data</item>
        <item>Delete individual entries or whole cashbooks inside the app, or uninstall the app / clear its data from Android settings to remove everything stored on the device. Backup files you saved elsewhere are under your control.</item>
    </string-array>
